WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:02.239
(claps)

00:00:02.239 --> 00:00:03.341
- This ring is hurting.

00:00:03.341 --> 00:00:05.686
I got to bring it up or something.

00:00:05.686 --> 00:00:06.544
(swoosh)

00:00:06.544 --> 00:00:08.641
(bang)

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.540
Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.327
Today we're going to talk
about seven ways to build

00:00:12.327 --> 00:00:15.785
huge followings on social media quickly.

00:00:15.785 --> 00:00:18.452
(hip hop music)

00:00:23.936 --> 00:00:25.508
So I've been getting a lot
of questions from you guys

00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:27.469
about how to build an
audience on social media.

00:00:27.469 --> 00:00:29.249
How do you get people to
care about your content?

00:00:29.249 --> 00:00:30.970
How do you get people
to engage with the stuff

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:31.877
that you're making?

00:00:31.877 --> 00:00:35.518
And so today I'm going
to share with you my

00:00:35.518 --> 00:00:36.351
seven ways

00:00:37.488 --> 00:00:41.071
to be able to build
huge audiences quickly.

00:00:43.892 --> 00:00:46.033
Way number one is form alliances

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.529
and I like this strategy
not just for social media

00:00:48.529 --> 00:00:50.078
but in business as well.

00:00:50.078 --> 00:00:53.263
The fastest way to bring on an audience

00:00:53.263 --> 00:00:57.705
to build a base is not to go
after people one at a time,

00:00:57.705 --> 00:00:59.346
one at a time, one at a time.

00:00:59.346 --> 00:01:03.737
It's to find somebody who
already has your target market

00:01:03.737 --> 00:01:06.800
and find some way to
collaborate with them.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.219
Find a way that you can offer value,

00:01:08.219 --> 00:01:09.304
that you can help them out,

00:01:09.304 --> 00:01:11.736
build some kind of connections
so that they will help

00:01:11.736 --> 00:01:13.583
promote you to their base.

00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:15.137
There's a couple ways that I did it

00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:16.813
in the early days of my channel.

00:01:16.813 --> 00:01:19.593
One, as an example, I
made thank you videos.

00:01:19.593 --> 00:01:22.175
And so I looked at some
YouTubers that I looked up to.

00:01:22.175 --> 00:01:23.715
I looked at Darrell Hughes,

00:01:23.715 --> 00:01:24.953
and I looked at Tim Schmoyer,

00:01:24.953 --> 00:01:26.457
and I looked at Gary Vaynerchuk

00:01:26.457 --> 00:01:28.539
and then I though I like these guys,

00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:31.345
I'm consuming their content,
I'm enjoying their stuff

00:01:31.345 --> 00:01:33.935
and I'm being engaged on their videos.

00:01:33.935 --> 00:01:35.452
And I thought, I want to thank them.

00:01:35.452 --> 00:01:36.988
I'm going to make a
thank you video for them

00:01:36.988 --> 00:01:38.899
but not just me thanking them,

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:43.055
I reached out to all of
their most active subscribers

00:01:43.055 --> 00:01:44.533
and said hey I want to
make a thank you video

00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:45.732
for Tim Schmoyer,

00:01:45.732 --> 00:01:48.928
can you put together a
30 second quick thank you

00:01:48.928 --> 00:01:51.164
'cause you like him too and
I'm going to mash them up

00:01:51.164 --> 00:01:52.199
and put them together.

00:01:52.199 --> 00:01:53.149
- Thank you very much Tim.

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:55.800
- I just want to say thank you so much for

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.541
all the help you have given to me.

00:01:57.541 --> 00:01:59.674
- You've certainly made
a huge impact on my life

00:01:59.674 --> 00:02:01.352
and my channel and I'm incredibly grateful

00:02:01.352 --> 00:02:03.324
for your guidance.

00:02:03.324 --> 00:02:04.373
- Surprise!

00:02:04.373 --> 00:02:05.206
Hey.

00:02:05.206 --> 00:02:06.039
- It's a lot of work.

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:07.782
But you need to find a way to stand out.

00:02:07.782 --> 00:02:09.715
You need to find a way
to offer a lot of value.

00:02:09.715 --> 00:02:11.666
If you're just getting started,

00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:13.831
an interview with you
isn't really going to bring

00:02:13.831 --> 00:02:15.696
somebody big a lot of value.

00:02:15.696 --> 00:02:19.421
But doing a lot of work to
make a thank you video will.

00:02:19.421 --> 00:02:21.352
And so everybody recognized it.

00:02:21.352 --> 00:02:23.074
Everybody that I've done
it for was so grateful,

00:02:23.074 --> 00:02:25.186
so thankful and it created openings,

00:02:25.186 --> 00:02:26.724
it created opportunities for me

00:02:26.724 --> 00:02:28.331
to get a lot more exposure.

00:02:28.331 --> 00:02:31.998
With Tim, I did three
different guest videos

00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:36.136
on his channel back when his channel was

00:02:36.136 --> 00:02:36.999
bigger than mine.

00:02:36.999 --> 00:02:38.896
I did three opportunities on his channel.

00:02:38.896 --> 00:02:40.099
He's been on my channel.

00:02:40.099 --> 00:02:43.167
We've done mastermind groups
and other projects together

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:45.217
and opened up a lot of
opportunities for us.

00:02:45.217 --> 00:02:48.943
So find people who already
have your target audience.

00:02:48.943 --> 00:02:49.932
They could be huge,

00:02:49.932 --> 00:02:51.198
they could also be smaller.

00:02:51.198 --> 00:02:53.371
And find a way to help them.

00:02:53.371 --> 00:02:55.417
Whatever it is that you are great at,

00:02:55.417 --> 00:02:58.252
find some way to add
value to their channel.

00:02:58.252 --> 00:02:59.710
Another quick example,

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:01.520
I like helping entrepreneurs.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.392
I've connected with other channels

00:03:03.392 --> 00:03:05.280
who are not in the entrepreneur space

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.752
but might need some entrepreneur help.

00:03:07.752 --> 00:03:09.896
Right, if somebody has a
YouTube channel talking about

00:03:09.896 --> 00:03:13.157
YouTubes like Sass, you
know a lot of their audience

00:03:13.157 --> 00:03:15.006
is going to still be entrepreneurs

00:03:15.006 --> 00:03:16.491
even though the topic of the channel

00:03:16.491 --> 00:03:17.685
is not entrepreneurship.

00:03:17.685 --> 00:03:19.527
So I can reach out and
say hey I'm an expert on

00:03:19.527 --> 00:03:21.380
entrepreneurship, I'd love
to collaborate on some kind

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:25.067
of video together to bring
value to your audience.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.681
Forming collaborations and
alliances is one of the

00:03:27.681 --> 00:03:31.848
fastest ways to build your
own audience for yourself.

00:03:33.869 --> 00:03:35.782
Number two is you need to be prolific.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:38.718
You need to create a ton of content.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.021
It does a couple things.

00:03:40.021 --> 00:03:41.620
One, it helps you get better.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.593
Right?

00:03:42.593 --> 00:03:44.823
The more you practice,
the better you'll get.

00:03:44.823 --> 00:03:47.382
The quantity leads to the quality.

00:03:47.382 --> 00:03:49.771
You can't just put up one
YouTube video and expect to

00:03:49.771 --> 00:03:50.709
be great.

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:52.126
Your first YouTube video is probably

00:03:52.126 --> 00:03:53.202
going to be pretty bad

00:03:53.202 --> 00:03:54.718
'cause you've never done a video before

00:03:54.718 --> 00:03:55.880
and the lighting will suck,

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.134
and the audio will suck,

00:03:57.134 --> 00:03:58.059
and the editing will suck,

00:03:58.059 --> 00:04:00.573
and you, your message,
your message will suck.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:01.985
You know, 'cause you never had practice.

00:04:01.985 --> 00:04:02.848
Be prolific.

00:04:02.848 --> 00:04:04.642
Get really, really, really good.

00:04:04.642 --> 00:04:06.888
I got better at YouTube and I became

00:04:06.888 --> 00:04:09.399
the best at the agency that I'm with

00:04:09.399 --> 00:04:10.346
from being the worst

00:04:10.346 --> 00:04:12.748
in a couple of months 'cause
I did videos every day.

00:04:12.748 --> 00:04:13.858
'Cause I grinded it out.

00:04:13.858 --> 00:04:15.321
Because I practiced and I improved.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.756
And if you go back on my channel,

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:19.013
go back six years ago,

00:04:19.013 --> 00:04:21.607
and you'll see how boring and stiff I was

00:04:21.607 --> 00:04:23.534
compared to how I am today.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.876
- Hi I'm Evan Carmichael,
welcome to another edition

00:04:25.876 --> 00:04:26.858
of Ask Evan.

00:04:26.858 --> 00:04:29.636
This is my first post of the
year for Telesox Business

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.051
and we're starting a new series,

00:04:31.051 --> 00:04:32.428
it's called The Challenge Series.

00:04:32.428 --> 00:04:34.686
We're going to be answering
the questions of entrepreneurs.

00:04:34.686 --> 00:04:37.268
And how did it go from there to here?

00:04:37.268 --> 00:04:38.258
Just practice.

00:04:38.258 --> 00:04:40.185
A lot of the points, a lot of the messages

00:04:40.185 --> 00:04:41.666
are the same.

00:04:41.666 --> 00:04:44.812
But my delivery is
better because I've done

00:04:44.812 --> 00:04:48.095
three and a half thousand
videos on my channel

00:04:48.095 --> 00:04:49.540
and most of them are public.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.324
So you need to be prolific to get better.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:54.358
You need to be prolific to
start attracting attention

00:04:54.358 --> 00:04:57.075
when you create a video or
a post on a certain topic.

00:04:57.075 --> 00:04:59.132
People who like that will find you,

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.311
or when you do collaborations
with other people,

00:05:01.311 --> 00:05:02.489
see point number one,

00:05:02.489 --> 00:05:04.630
they're going to come to your
channel and give you a shot.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:05.463
Right?

00:05:05.463 --> 00:05:07.079
Oh he just did a collaboration
with that person,

00:05:07.079 --> 00:05:08.611
okay let me go check out his channel.

00:05:08.611 --> 00:05:10.301
You have to have content on there.

00:05:10.301 --> 00:05:13.811
Why am I going to subscribe
to your channel or follow you

00:05:13.811 --> 00:05:15.426
if you don't have great content?

00:05:15.426 --> 00:05:16.259
Right?

00:05:16.259 --> 00:05:17.571
The collaboration gives you the opening,

00:05:17.571 --> 00:05:18.826
it gives you some awareness.

00:05:18.826 --> 00:05:20.519
They're going to hit your page.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.259
They're going to see
your Instagram messages,

00:05:22.259 --> 00:05:23.310
or your Facebook posts,

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.039
or your Tweets or your videos,

00:05:25.039 --> 00:05:27.423
there has to be something
there that is quality

00:05:27.423 --> 00:05:29.323
that people are going
to want to consume it,

00:05:29.323 --> 00:05:31.540
and they consume it again
and again and again.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.113
You have to be prolific.

00:05:34.113 --> 00:05:34.946
Create

00:05:34.946 --> 00:05:36.133
constantly.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:38.488
One video a week is not enough.

00:05:38.488 --> 00:05:40.956
One post a week is not enough.

00:05:40.956 --> 00:05:41.956
Be prolific.

00:05:45.686 --> 00:05:47.597
Number three is have a message.

00:05:47.597 --> 00:05:50.076
This ties into my book
Your One Word but I believe

00:05:50.076 --> 00:05:52.909
everybody has a message
and that has to come out.

00:05:52.909 --> 00:05:54.614
Because people buy why
you're doing something

00:05:54.614 --> 00:05:56.128
much more than what you're doing.

00:05:56.128 --> 00:05:57.984
My message is Believe, it's my one word,

00:05:57.984 --> 00:05:59.966
it oozes out of everything that I do.

00:05:59.966 --> 00:06:02.339
And as a result I'm
known as the believe guy,

00:06:02.339 --> 00:06:03.888
especially for entrepreneurs.

00:06:03.888 --> 00:06:05.607
And whenever people see the word believe,

00:06:05.607 --> 00:06:06.875
they're thinking of me.

00:06:06.875 --> 00:06:09.659
I want people to be
able to think about you

00:06:09.659 --> 00:06:11.837
and your mission and not just the content

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:13.140
that you're creating.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.181
Because you might put out one great post,

00:06:15.181 --> 00:06:17.000
fine, great they consume it.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.823
I want to know why you're doing it.

00:06:18.823 --> 00:06:20.397
I want to know the mission that you're on

00:06:20.397 --> 00:06:22.085
to make the world a better place

00:06:22.085 --> 00:06:23.447
and if I'm on that same mission,

00:06:23.447 --> 00:06:26.261
I'm going to consume
everything that you create.

00:06:26.261 --> 00:06:28.061
I want to watch every
video that you put up.

00:06:28.061 --> 00:06:29.755
I want to see every Tweet that you push.

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.806
I want to see every Instagram
or Facebook picture.

00:06:31.806 --> 00:06:33.320
I want to see every
Snap that you're writing

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:34.768
'cause I need more of that.

00:06:34.768 --> 00:06:36.668
If you want more believe in your life,

00:06:36.668 --> 00:06:38.073
you're going to love my content,

00:06:38.073 --> 00:06:40.120
you're going to want to
consume as much as possible.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.562
'Cause you need to believe in yourself

00:06:41.562 --> 00:06:42.886
and your mission more.

00:06:42.886 --> 00:06:44.112
The same thing for you.

00:06:44.112 --> 00:06:45.357
What is your message?

00:06:45.357 --> 00:06:46.824
What are you trying to get out there?

00:06:46.824 --> 00:06:50.025
And does that ooze out of
every post that you put?

00:06:50.025 --> 00:06:51.410
Now if you hate believe,

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.462
that believe is stupid,
believe isn't for me,

00:06:53.462 --> 00:06:54.886
you're going to hate my content too.

00:06:54.886 --> 00:06:55.719
Right?

00:06:55.719 --> 00:06:56.938
Like you're not going to
want to watch anything,

00:06:56.938 --> 00:06:59.529
you're not watching anymore on this video

00:06:59.529 --> 00:07:01.901
'cause you don't like the
message, and that's fine.

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:04.627
I want people to love your message or not.

00:07:04.627 --> 00:07:06.920
I don't want you just
be another person doing

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:07.935
the same thing.

00:07:07.935 --> 00:07:10.027
Right, and so understanding
what your one word is,

00:07:10.027 --> 00:07:11.372
understanding what your message is,

00:07:11.372 --> 00:07:13.974
and then having that ooze
through every piece of content

00:07:13.974 --> 00:07:17.734
makes a huge, huge, huge,
huge, huge difference

00:07:17.734 --> 00:07:19.089
in the people that you'll attract

00:07:19.089 --> 00:07:22.506
and the shareability of all your content.

00:07:24.271 --> 00:07:26.270
Number four is model success.

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:28.052
Whenever you don't know
how to do something,

00:07:28.052 --> 00:07:29.855
this has been my default go-to.

00:07:29.855 --> 00:07:31.855
If I don't know how to do something,

00:07:31.855 --> 00:07:33.100
I try to model success.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:35.595
I try to find somebody who's
done what I want to do,

00:07:35.595 --> 00:07:36.868
or close to it,

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:38.262
and see what worked for them,

00:07:38.262 --> 00:07:40.415
what are they doing that is really working

00:07:40.415 --> 00:07:43.070
and how can I take
pieces of it to help me.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:46.823
And it's not being the next Steve Jobs,

00:07:46.823 --> 00:07:48.553
or being the next Evan Carmichael,

00:07:48.553 --> 00:07:50.422
or being the next Gary Vaynerchuk

00:07:50.422 --> 00:07:52.291
or whoever it is that you look up to.

00:07:52.291 --> 00:07:55.019
It's taking pieces from
them to help you be the best

00:07:55.019 --> 00:07:56.137
version of yourself.

00:07:56.137 --> 00:07:58.301
And so every time I've modeled success,

00:07:58.301 --> 00:08:00.604
I couldn't do exactly what
that other person was doing

00:08:00.604 --> 00:08:02.608
because it didn't feel right to me.

00:08:02.608 --> 00:08:04.505
Not because I'm stealing their ideas,

00:08:04.505 --> 00:08:06.820
just because the way
that it worked for them

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.104
I needed to tweak.

00:08:08.104 --> 00:08:09.609
I always needed to tweak it.

00:08:09.609 --> 00:08:12.310
But I understood their
strategy and once I tweaked it,

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:14.222
I could make it my own
and that's when I started

00:08:14.222 --> 00:08:15.217
having success.

00:08:15.217 --> 00:08:18.430
Where I had a media coach
helping me at my agency

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.213
to be better, we'd review videos

00:08:20.213 --> 00:08:23.221
and she would tell me every
week something to work on.

00:08:23.221 --> 00:08:25.183
And I always try, like
if you give me a task,

00:08:25.183 --> 00:08:26.916
I'll try, I'll work it, I'll try to do it,

00:08:26.916 --> 00:08:29.506
but it never felt perfectly right

00:08:29.506 --> 00:08:31.264
because that's her view.

00:08:31.264 --> 00:08:33.472
That's what she would do.

00:08:33.472 --> 00:08:35.789
That's what she's seen
work in her own stuff.

00:08:35.789 --> 00:08:37.410
And I can't be her.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.879
And I always needed to
tweak it to make it my own

00:08:39.879 --> 00:08:41.532
but there was always a growth lesson.

00:08:41.532 --> 00:08:44.038
Everything she told me,
I could always find a way

00:08:44.038 --> 00:08:46.264
after some uncomfortableness of trying

00:08:46.264 --> 00:08:47.978
to then say I like that,

00:08:47.978 --> 00:08:49.782
I'm going to go here and do this.

00:08:49.782 --> 00:08:51.823
And so whenever you don't know what to do,

00:08:51.823 --> 00:08:52.915
model success.

00:08:52.915 --> 00:08:53.923
Find the people who've done it,

00:08:53.923 --> 00:08:56.756
bring it to work for your company.

00:08:58.979 --> 00:09:00.709
Number five is get in the media.

00:09:00.709 --> 00:09:02.854
More, more, more, more

00:09:02.854 --> 00:09:06.113
traditional media are looking
to the people on social media

00:09:06.113 --> 00:09:07.118
as experts.

00:09:07.118 --> 00:09:09.440
So whatever it is that
you're an expert in,

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.456
and you should be an expert at something,

00:09:11.456 --> 00:09:13.343
you have expert opinions on things.

00:09:13.343 --> 00:09:15.501
And any time somebody's
writing a story on something,

00:09:15.501 --> 00:09:17.239
they're always looking for an expert.

00:09:17.239 --> 00:09:19.277
And so I'd be looking
at who the reporter is

00:09:19.277 --> 00:09:21.990
in traditional media that
are covering your space.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.700
And then any time they
write a story about it,

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:24.800
you're reaching out.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:26.738
And you can give some commentary on it.

00:09:26.738 --> 00:09:28.370
And the next time they write
a story they're going to

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.237
remember you and what you're all about,

00:09:30.237 --> 00:09:31.290
and what you're doing.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:34.346
Understand that reporters
have a hard time.

00:09:34.346 --> 00:09:36.465
Reporters are not the
experts on a lot of things.

00:09:36.465 --> 00:09:38.630
They always need these
guest people to come in

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:40.674
and give them more insight and context

00:09:40.674 --> 00:09:41.892
to help their stories

00:09:41.892 --> 00:09:44.412
because they need a source for
every story that they write.

00:09:44.412 --> 00:09:48.228
If you are a credible source
that has great information,

00:09:48.228 --> 00:09:50.345
you're making their life easier.

00:09:50.345 --> 00:09:53.209
You're making the life
of that reporter easier.

00:09:53.209 --> 00:09:55.474
And they're going to come
back to you again, and again

00:09:55.474 --> 00:09:57.196
and again any time they have something

00:09:57.196 --> 00:09:58.276
that covers your niche.

00:09:58.276 --> 00:09:59.936
And so I'd be reaching out to reporters,

00:09:59.936 --> 00:10:01.229
especially if you're using social,

00:10:01.229 --> 00:10:04.026
most of them are on some
kind of social platform

00:10:04.026 --> 00:10:05.128
whether it's Twitter,

00:10:05.128 --> 00:10:07.510
whether it's Instagram,

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:08.926
whether it's LinkedIn,

00:10:08.926 --> 00:10:10.534
you can find them on social,

00:10:10.534 --> 00:10:12.295
it's way easier than ever before.

00:10:12.295 --> 00:10:14.194
Comment on their stories,
show yourself to be

00:10:14.194 --> 00:10:15.424
a successful expert,

00:10:15.424 --> 00:10:16.520
to know what you're talking about,

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:18.033
to add value to their content,

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:19.947
and then the next time
they're doing an interview

00:10:19.947 --> 00:10:21.713
they're going to be talking about you.

00:10:21.713 --> 00:10:24.546
You sharing your amazing opinions.

00:10:26.974 --> 00:10:28.726
Number six is get some help.

00:10:28.726 --> 00:10:30.622
I'm not a big believer in spending money

00:10:30.622 --> 00:10:31.692
until you're making money,

00:10:31.692 --> 00:10:33.290
but if you found the
path to be able to make

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:34.603
some money from this,

00:10:34.603 --> 00:10:36.292
whether you're doing social content

00:10:36.292 --> 00:10:38.608
and that helps drive business for you

00:10:38.608 --> 00:10:40.651
either selling product or services,

00:10:40.651 --> 00:10:42.460
as soon as you start making some money

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:44.217
from your social path,

00:10:44.217 --> 00:10:45.490
then bring on some help.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:47.339
Bring on people to give you assistance.

00:10:47.339 --> 00:10:50.789
For me, on YouTube, the
first person I hired

00:10:50.789 --> 00:10:51.994
was an editor.

00:10:51.994 --> 00:10:54.117
I was doing everything at the start.

00:10:54.117 --> 00:10:55.208
And I had money.

00:10:55.208 --> 00:10:57.659
I just don't like spending
money until I'm making it.

00:10:57.659 --> 00:10:59.872
I could've taken money and started it all

00:10:59.872 --> 00:11:01.414
and got the lights and gear and camera

00:11:01.414 --> 00:11:02.251
and all that stuff.

00:11:02.251 --> 00:11:03.909
But I didn't know if I was
going to stick with it.

00:11:03.909 --> 00:11:05.970
And the worst that you can
do is spend a ton of money

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.705
on something, try it twice,

00:11:07.705 --> 00:11:08.963
and then give up on it and you're sitting

00:11:08.963 --> 00:11:11.203
with all this expensive
gear in your basement

00:11:11.203 --> 00:11:13.083
that you can't get rid of.

00:11:13.083 --> 00:11:15.720
And so I was the camera
man, I was the researcher,

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:18.016
I was in front and behind the camera,

00:11:18.016 --> 00:11:21.500
I was editing, I was
doing all the analytics,

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.683
everything, I was everything

00:11:22.683 --> 00:11:24.035
for my YouTube channel to start.

00:11:24.035 --> 00:11:25.872
And as soon as I started
to get some traction,

00:11:25.872 --> 00:11:27.636
and I was generating sales for me,

00:11:27.636 --> 00:11:30.203
I hired an editor and
that allowed me to move

00:11:30.203 --> 00:11:32.696
from a video a week to a video a day.

00:11:32.696 --> 00:11:35.176
And now we're up to three
to five videos a day

00:11:35.176 --> 00:11:36.376
depending on the day,

00:11:36.376 --> 00:11:38.025
because I built up my team.

00:11:38.025 --> 00:11:39.934
We've got more people working for me.

00:11:39.934 --> 00:11:43.217
And so thinking about what
you're really great at.

00:11:43.217 --> 00:11:44.226
Are you great at designing?

00:11:44.226 --> 00:11:45.172
Are you great at writing?

00:11:45.172 --> 00:11:46.167
Are you great at copy?

00:11:46.167 --> 00:11:47.685
Are you great at being
in front of the camera?

00:11:47.685 --> 00:11:48.810
Are you great at editing?

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.146
Are you great at strategizing?

00:11:50.146 --> 00:11:52.225
What is your strengths?

00:11:52.225 --> 00:11:54.167
And as soon as you can afford it,

00:11:54.167 --> 00:11:57.205
bringing on people to
compliment your strengths

00:11:57.205 --> 00:11:59.438
to take over your weaknesses so you can be

00:11:59.438 --> 00:12:02.684
even more prolific with
higher quality stuff

00:12:02.684 --> 00:12:04.434
that you can put out.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.414
And number seven is you
have to be passionate.

00:12:09.414 --> 00:12:11.267
Whenever you are
passionate about the things

00:12:11.267 --> 00:12:13.530
that you are doing, you
will get better results.

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:16.555
If you are creating content
because somebody else

00:12:16.555 --> 00:12:17.857
is creating content,

00:12:17.857 --> 00:12:19.570
or you're posting something
up because you think

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:21.146
it's going to be a hot thing,

00:12:21.146 --> 00:12:23.185
but you don't have any interest in it,

00:12:23.185 --> 00:12:24.952
it's not going to work.

00:12:24.952 --> 00:12:26.541
You're not going to get the right people.

00:12:26.541 --> 00:12:29.725
You have to create the
things that make you excited.

00:12:29.725 --> 00:12:32.269
That you would want to show
your kids and grandkids.

00:12:32.269 --> 00:12:34.315
That should be the acid test.

00:12:34.315 --> 00:12:36.180
If you're making a piece of content,

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:39.214
whether it's a video or
a picture or a blog post

00:12:39.214 --> 00:12:40.047
or whatever it is,

00:12:40.047 --> 00:12:41.498
you're making a piece of content,

00:12:41.498 --> 00:12:44.229
make something that you
want to show your grandkids

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:46.045
and say look what I made.

00:12:46.045 --> 00:12:49.927
And if that passion comes
through into every piece

00:12:49.927 --> 00:12:51.298
of content that you're creating,

00:12:51.298 --> 00:12:55.448
I promise you, you are going
to attract like-minded people

00:12:55.448 --> 00:12:58.369
who also love the work that you're doing,

00:12:58.369 --> 00:13:00.524
and will be your ambassadors for you.

00:13:00.524 --> 00:13:02.234
Where if all you're trying to do is

00:13:02.234 --> 00:13:04.212
chase click bait titles,

00:13:04.212 --> 00:13:06.244
and you don't actually care
that much about those topics,

00:13:06.244 --> 00:13:07.848
you'll get some people coming in,

00:13:07.848 --> 00:13:09.425
but they're not going to stick.

00:13:09.425 --> 00:13:10.822
They're not going to join your movement.

00:13:10.822 --> 00:13:12.222
They're not going to
really want to follow you.

00:13:12.222 --> 00:13:15.621
They're not going to really
share all of your future stuff

00:13:15.621 --> 00:13:17.936
because you're not deeply
connected to the message.

00:13:17.936 --> 00:13:20.686
And so it's super important
that when you're creating

00:13:20.686 --> 00:13:23.835
this content you feel
connected to every single piece

00:13:23.835 --> 00:13:27.728
and you want to show it to your grandkids.

00:13:27.728 --> 00:13:31.328
So those are my seven tips
on how to build a massive

00:13:31.328 --> 00:13:33.457
audience super quickly.

00:13:33.457 --> 00:13:35.305
I'd love to know what do you guys think?

00:13:35.305 --> 00:13:36.596
What was your favorite tip?

00:13:36.596 --> 00:13:39.752
What is most relevant and
applicable to your business

00:13:39.752 --> 00:13:42.147
that you're going to start
immediately working on?

00:13:42.147 --> 00:13:43.575
Did I miss some?

00:13:43.575 --> 00:13:45.393
Is there an eight, nine, ten that you guys

00:13:45.393 --> 00:13:46.646
want to add to the list?

00:13:46.646 --> 00:13:47.822
Leave it in the comments below,

00:13:47.822 --> 00:13:50.223
super curious to figure out
what you guys are going to say.

00:13:50.223 --> 00:13:52.351
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Danijel.

00:13:52.351 --> 00:13:54.754
Danijel, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:13:54.754 --> 00:13:55.918
Your One Word,

00:13:55.918 --> 00:13:57.735
for posting an awesome review on Amazon,

00:13:57.735 --> 00:13:59.559
along with the two pictures.

00:13:59.559 --> 00:14:02.165
I really, really, really
appreciate the love and support

00:14:02.165 --> 00:14:03.802
and hope you're enjoying the book.

00:14:03.802 --> 00:14:05.140
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.426
I believe in you.

00:14:06.426 --> 00:14:08.466
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:14:08.466 --> 00:14:10.521
and whatever your one word is.

00:14:10.521 --> 00:14:11.976
Much love.

00:14:11.976 --> 00:14:13.476
I'll see you soon.

